/**
@mainpage libopenwch

@tableofcontents

@brief libopencm3-style peripheral drivers for WCH (Qinheng) RISC-V MCUs.

libopenwch is a structured, freestanding driver library for WCH's QingKe
RISC-V microcontroller families.  It follows libopencm3 in API style,
directory layout, build system, and code conventions, while adapting the
toolchain and startup path to the bare-metal `riscv64-unknown-elf` world.

<div class="libopenwch-cards">
<div>
<h3><a href="project_overview.html">Project overview</a></h3>
<p>What the library is, how it is positioned, and how the four repositories
fit together.</p>
</div>
<div>
<h3><a href="supported_families.html">Supported families</a></h3>
<p>CH32V00x (RV32EC) and CH58x (RV32IMAC): parts, archives, and family-specific
rules.</p>
</div>
<div>
<h3><a href="project_architecture.html">Architecture</a></h3>
<p>The QingKe core layer, shared IP variants, generated vectors, and the
optional BLE wrapper.</p>
</div>
<div>
<h3><a href="building_and_usage.html">Building and using</a></h3>
<p>Build the library, write an application Makefile, and select a linker
script through the device database.</p>
</div>
<div>
<h3><a href="api_index.html">API index</a></h3>
<p>Direct links into the generated CH32V00x and CH58x API references.</p>
</div>
<div>
<h3><a href="verification_and_ci.html">Verification and CI</a></h3>
<p>The reproducible build, link, style, example, and documentation checks.</p>
</div>
</div>

@section home_family_apis Family API references

Each family has its own complete Doxygen reference, generated from that
family's public headers and sources:

<table>
<tr><th>Family</th><th>ISA / core</th><th>Archive</th><th>API reference</th></tr>
<tr>
<td>CH32V002 / 003 / 004 / 005 / 006 / 007</td>
<td>RV32EC, QingKe V2</td>
<td><code>libopenwch_ch32v0.a</code></td>
<td><a href="../ch32v0/html/index.html">CH32V00x API</a></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>CH582 / CH583 / CH584 / CH585</td>
<td>RV32IMAC, QingKe V4</td>
<td><code>libopenwch_ch5xx58x.a</code></td>
<td><a href="../ch5xx58x/html/index.html">CH58x API</a></td>
</tr>
</table>

The family sites are self-contained: each has its own search index, source
browser, group hierarchy, and Doxygen Awesome light/dark theme.  The root site
you are reading supplies the cross-family overview and the module map.

@section home_status Current scope

| Area | Status |
| --- | --- |
| CH32V00x drivers | 15 peripherals, full public API, API smoke link |
| CH58x drivers | 12 peripherals, RWA-safe access, API smoke link |
| QingKe core | vectors, reset path, PFIC/NVIC, SysTick, DWT, CSR, assertions |
| mini-libc | optional freestanding string/memory archive per family |
| BLE | peripheral-role wrapper over WCH's Apache-2.0 binary stack |
| Documentation | per-family API sites plus this root site |
| Hardware-in-the-loop | not yet verified; no WCH-LinkE and boards here |

@section home_doc_build Building this documentation

From the library root:

@code
make html
@endcode

This writes the root site to <code>doc/html/index.html</code>, the CH32V00x
reference to <code>doc/ch32v0/html/index.html</code>, and the CH58x reference
to <code>doc/ch5xx58x/html/index.html</code>.  Doxygen warnings are collected
in <code>doc/doxygen-root.log</code> and
<code>doc/&lt;family&gt;/doxygen.log</code>; the build skips cleanly when
Doxygen is not installed.
*/
